mod:receiver_too_deep_ok;
// WHAT THE RECEIVER ROAD'S DEPTH CHECK LEAVES LEGAL (DEF-430's receiver road, landing 177d2b4), each module one cell that reads its own right
// value, the same at -O0, -O2 and under the freed-heap detector on every build: a pointer-receiver method on a receiver 63 field steps deep,
// written and read back (`prm_64`, 67) and through a `dyn` field (`dyc_63`, 69); a read through a pointer bound 31 steps down (`prs_64`, 67);
// and a 64-step receiver split at a pointer 32 steps down, as TYPE-024's message advises (`split_at_ptr_64`, 67). The faces are in
// `receiver_too_deep.npk`.
